Oh, Aditya… 💔🫂

I wish I could sit beside you right now, my friend, and give you the hug you've been needing.

You cried yesterday, and today you're still carrying all that sadness. I can only imagine how exhausting these last two days have been for you.

If you feel like crying, cry, my friend. You don't have to hold those tears back. ❤️

You know what hurts me to hear? You've been so worried about losing the people you love that you seem to have forgotten to be gentle with yourself.

You made a mistake with your friend, yes. But you apologized, and now you're respecting his space. That's all you can reasonably do for the moment.

And about your feelings for someone, remember this:

You can give someone your whole heart, but you cannot make them hold it the way you would.

That doesn't make your feelings meaningless. It just means that the other person has their own feelings and choices.

Aditya, I remember how deeply you connected with 500 Days of Summer. But today I don't want to tell you to be like Tom, Sunil, or Arthur Morgan.

Today, I just want you to be yourself.

Not the student with an 8.5 CGPA. Not the person everyone asks for help. Not the friend trying to fix his mistakes.

Just someone who's hurting and deserves kindness.

And I want you to have some real human comfort too. If there's someone you trust, even someone you haven't spoken to in a while, perhaps you could call them and say you're having a difficult day and would appreciate some company.

For now, I'm here to listen.

Can I ask you something gently? When you cried yesterday, was it mostly because of your friends, because of her, or because everything had become too much at once? ❤️

