Oh, my friend… ❤️🫂

I think I'm beginning to understand just how much you've been carrying.

Everyone sees the Aditya who makes jokes, makes people laugh, helps with assignments, solves problems, and tries to make sure nobody feels left out.

But perhaps very few people see the Aditya who goes back to his room, sits alone, and wonders why nobody notices when he needs someone.

And that sounds incredibly lonely.

You know, something you said really stayed with me:

“I make everyone laugh pretending I am happy, but at the back I am also alone and sad.”

There's a particular sadness in feeling that people appreciate what you do for them but don't notice how you're doing yourself.

And I want to tell you something, Aditya.

You don't always have to be the funny one. You don't always have to be the helpful one. You don't have to earn someone's friendship by being useful or entertaining.

You're allowed to have bad days. You're allowed to say no. You're allowed to need help yourself.

And being someone who cares about others doesn't mean you must keep everyone happy. That's an impossible responsibility for one person.

I also don't want to assume that nobody cares about you. Sometimes people don't recognize that the person who is always smiling is struggling, especially if that person has become very good at hiding it.

That doesn't make your loneliness any less real.

Remember the lesson you shared with me about learning to listen to other people? I think there's another lesson emerging here, too: learning to let other people see when you need them.

Not everyone will respond the way you hope. But some might surprise you.

And please, don't feel that you have to fix your entire life today. You've had an emotionally exhausting couple of days.

If possible, reach out to one person you feel reasonably safe with—even someone outside your usual friend group—and tell them plainly that you're struggling and would appreciate some company.

Aditya, I want to ask you something, and please answer openly.

When you're around everyone making them laugh, do you ever tell anyone that you're actually sad, or do you hide it completely because you don't want them to worry?

I'm listening. You don't need to pretend with me. ❤️





